      "content": "I'd say pushing the limits of caffeine and green tea extract can be beneficial for fat burning, but only up to a point. Taking an additional 500-750mg of green tea extract, like you mentioned, might not be a bad idea, as it can further enhance thermogenesis. However, I'd caution against exceeding 1500-2000mg of green tea extract per day, as it may lead to adverse effects like jitteriness, anxiety, and stomach upset.\n\nAs for caffeine, I'd recommend not exceeding 600-800mg per day, especially if you're doing high-intensity cardio. Going beyond that can lead to jitters, anxiety, and an increased heart rate, which might not be ideal for optimal fat burning.\n\nBut, let's be real, the real key to maximizing fat burning is not just about the amount of supplements you take, but also about your diet, exercise routine, and overall lifestyle. So, don't just rely on caffeine and green tea extract – make sure you're fueling your body with the right foods and getting enough rest, too.",
